&lt;p&gt;Lovable's marketing pricing page didn't print dollar amounts when I checked on 28 October 2026. The numbers are in Lovable's own docs: the Subscription plans page and the Credits and usage page. Here's what each plan costs, what a credit costs you, and when it's worth paying.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  TL;DR
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;You are...&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Best plan&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Cost&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Trying Lovable out&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Free&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;$0: 5 build credits a day, capped at 30 a month&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Building one real project&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pro, 100 credits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;$25/mo, or $250/yr (~$21/mo)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A student or teacher&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pro, 100 credits, 50% off&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Half of $25 for up to 12 months&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Running out every month&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A bigger Pro tier&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Same $0.25/credit up to 800 credits, a bit less above that&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Needing team controls&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;From $50/mo for 100 credits&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Short version: Pro is the plan to buy. Bigger Pro tiers just buy more credits, not more features.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Free plan
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;5 build credits a day, up to 30 a month.&lt;/strong&gt; On Free, that cap is hit after 6 days of daily use (6 × 5 = 30). Then nothing until the 1st.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;20 Cloud credits, 4 AI credits and 1 connector credit a month, for running your app's backend and AI features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fine for testing an idea. A real app will hit the cap in the first week.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Pro: you're buying credits
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Every Pro tier is the same plan with a bigger monthly balance. I added the cost per credit so you can see where the discount kicks in:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
